\section{Conclusion}
\label{sec:conclusion}
\vspace{-2pt}

\looseness=-2 We presented ACR-VLA, an adaptive inference-time correction pipeline for frozen flow-matching VLAs. A $K{=}2$ pairwise $L_2$ uncertainty probe ($\rho{=}0.9979$) gates lightweight CRM correction, achieving $18.3$\% Object / $35.0$\% Spatial on SmolVLA ($+$7.3 / $+$5.6\,pp vs.\ VLA-only) while matching fixed-$K{=}10$ with 80\% fewer VLA forward passes. Systematic analysis confirms that learned correction contributes 55--78\% of the gain, while multi-sampling provides the enabling centering condition.
\textbf{Limitations.}\enspace We present initial cross-VLA validation on $\pi_{0.5}$ (3.6B) in Appendix~\ref{sec:cross_vla}; broader generalization across VLA families and real-robot transfer remain future work. The CRM requires task-specific calibration data and stochastic sample diversity, excluding tokenized VLAs (Appendix~\ref{sec:applicability}). AI tools assisted with code and manuscript.

